#!/usr/bin/env python
"""
train_morphology_predictor.py
=============================

Train and evaluate small-data morphology predictors for hydrothermally
grown ZnO using DOE synthesis parameters.

Inputs
------
RPM
pH
Time (h)
Temperature (°C)

Targets
-------
ZnO coverage (%)
Mean nanosheet width (µm)

Experimental structure
----------------------
SEM images are repeated measurements nested within 9 independent DOE Runs.
Therefore, model validation is performed at the Run level using strict
Leave-One-Run-Out (LORO) cross-validation.

Models
------
- Linear Regression
- Ridge Regression
- Bayesian Ridge
- Random Forest
- Extra Trees
- Gradient Boosting
- Additive Gaussian Process
- Weighted ensemble of the candidate models

The script also performs hierarchical bootstrap analysis for the selected
predictor and saves model-comparison tables, LORO predictions, figures,
training-domain metadata, and reproducibility information.
"""

